ID: B3-Ch10c-Available
TEXT:

 "I think he was the least bad choice available at the time."

"Oh?" Eiden's brow arches. "I was under the impression your company held considerable sway over Ollendor's succession. Am I to understand your backing rested solely on him being the least dreadful option?"

"Pretty much," I say with a shrug.

"I see," Eiden says.

Silence settles between us for several seconds until I break it.

"Is that all you wanted to ask?"

"On that subject, yes," Eiden says.

"And the second matter?" Kate asks, her brow furrowing.

"A timely question, Kate of the Beacon of Hope," Eiden says. "This concerns you above all others. Waiting for your little band to reach your next milestone grew tedious, so I came to quicken your pace. Your upcoming encounter interests me as much as it does you."

"Why would our next destination interest you?" Kate asks.

"...You do not know where you are going?" Eiden's eyes remain closed, but his head tilts in genuine surprise.

He turns toward Melindra. Her posture stiffens instantly.

 "Melindra, you have not told them?" Eiden asks.

"I was going to!" Melindra says, her voice jumping an octave. "I was waiting for the right moment!"

"There is no time like the present," Eiden says smoothly.

"Melindra, what is this?" Kate steps forward. "Who are you taking us to? What does this have to do with me?"

"Kate, listen to me," Melindra says, hands fluttering in front of her chest. "First, stay calm. Promise me you will stay calm."

"Fine," Kate says. "I promise."

"Right," Melindra takes a ragged breath. "When we struck our deal in Ollendor, I knew nothing about artificial mages or the Beacon of Hope. I only learned about all that later, listening to you talk around the fire."

"Understood," Kate says. "Why bring it up now?"

"Because..." Melindra swallows hard. "The contact with the pinecone detector... my acquaintance... she is--"

